  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "correctness",
    "affected_api": "pandas.Timedelta",
    "observed_behavior": "Timedelta and to_timedelta raise a bare OverflowError for inf/-inf float input, and for overflowing round floats or ints with a coarse unit such as unit='s' (e.g. Timedelta(1e19, unit='s') and Timedelta(10**19, unit='s')). errors='coerce' cannot catch this bare OverflowError, so NaT is not returned.",
    "expected_behavior": "OutOfBoundsTimedelta (a ValueError) is raised instead, so errors='coerce' returns NaT.",
    "manifestation": "exception",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "float input of inf or -inf passed to Timedelta or to_timedelta",
      "overflowing round float or integer with a coarse unit such as unit='s' (e.g. Timedelta(1e19, unit='s'))",
      "errors='coerce' passed to to_timedelta"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "Timedelta(np.inf)",
        "buggy_output": "bare OverflowError",
        "expected_output": "OutOfBoundsTimedelta",
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "PR body and test_float_inf_raises"
      },
      {
        "input": "Timedelta(-np.inf)",
        "buggy_output": "bare OverflowError",
        "expected_output": "OutOfBoundsTimedelta",
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "test_float_inf_raises parametrized over np.inf and -np.inf"
      },
      {
        "input": "to_timedelta(np.inf)",
        "buggy_output": "bare OverflowError",
        "expected_output": "OutOfBoundsTimedelta",
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "test_float_inf_raises"
      },
      {
        "input": "to_timedelta(np.inf, errors='coerce')",
        "buggy_output": "bare OverflowError (not caught, NaT not returned)",
        "expected_output": "NaT",
        "value_kind": "property",
        "source": "test_"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": []
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": null,
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": "Non-finite inf/-inf floats; overflowing round floats such as Timedelta(1e19, unit=\"s\") and Timedelta(10**19, unit=\"s\")",
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Passage: Non-finite float input (inf/-inf) was routed through int(item), raising a bare OverflowError that errors=\"coerce\" could not catch; fix uses is_integer() so such values fall through to _numeric_to_td64ns yielding OutOfBoundsTimedelta (or NaT under coerce).",
      "Passage: float(\"inf\").is_integer() is False, so non-finite floats fall through to _numeric_to_td64ns and raise OutOfBoundsTimedelta (a ValueError), so coerce gives NaT.",
      "Passage: Pandas 2.3.x gave NaT/OutOfBoundsTimedelta for these inputs, per the PR body; the bare OverflowError was a regression in the reported behavior.",
      "Passage: Timedelta(10**19, unit=\"s\") and Timedelta(1e19, unit=\"s\") went through np.timedelta64(value, unit) which raises a bare OverflowError; now wrapped to raise OutOfBoundsTimedelta with message 'Cannot cast ... without overflow.'",
      "Passage: test_float_inf_raises parametrized over np.inf and -np.inf expects OutOfBoundsTimedelta from Timedelta(val) and to_timedelta(val), and to_timedelta(val, errors=\"coerce\") is NaT.",
      "Passage: test_round_float_overflow_unit expects Timedelta(1e19, unit=\"s\") to raise OutOfBoundsTimedelta.",
      "Passage: NaN never reaches this branch because it is caught earlier by checknull_with_nat_and_na (PR body).",
      "Passage: The related issue text concerns datetime/timedelta resolution (ns default) and the unit keyword interpreting input rather than the output unit; the passages do not state a mathematical formula or expected numeric values for the violated property."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "The passages do not give a dtype, precision, or explicit tolerance; these are left null rather than inferred.",
      "Exact error message text is only partially given (\"without overflow\" match substring) and the full message is not stated.",
      "The PR body is truncated, so the complete set of changes is not visible.",
      "Issue discussion about ns vs us default resolution is a separate design question and not a verified numerical reproduction value."
    ]
  },
